    "title": "The Tropical Valuation Rank of Digit-Preserving Factorizations",
    "description": "Define the base-b digit count nu_b(n) = number of base-b digits of n. On a same-digit factorization v = x*y (digits of x and y are jointly a permutation of digits of v), nu_b is perfectly additive: nu_b(v) = nu_b(x) + nu_b(y), so nu_b is a homomorphism from the multiplicative monoid of such factorizations into the tropical (max-plus) semiring. Conjecture: for a fixed base b, the set of integers admitting a k-fold digit-preserving factorization forms a tropical-linear stratification by total valuation, and the number of distinct tropical ranks achievable by 2n-digit integers grows linearly in n. Approach: extend digit-length additivity to k factors, build the induced grading on the monoid of factorizations, and count achievable rank vectors combinatorially.",
